	"bugClass": {
		"id": "dynamic-tool-context-recharge",
		"title": "Dynamic tools cause context churn and repeated input charging",
		"cause": "A worker starts with only some tools restricted while account or user MCP tools continue loading or changing during the session, causing context growth and tool-list churn. Separately, admission logic fingerprints the entire tools block as one unit, so adding one tool makes every existing tool appear new and recharge as input.",
		"criteria": "Classify a site when either mechanism is present: (1) a worker launch restricts built-in tools but leaves account/user MCP servers enabled for mid-session loading or updates; or (2) a pre-request context or cost gate hashes or fingerprints the complete tools block as a single field and treats a change to that block as new input for all tools. Either mechanism alone qualifies.",
